  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.104,
            0.17,
            0.12
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "CIRCLES"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.863,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "149"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.094,
            0.139,
            0.562,
            0.178
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Theorem 10.2 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The lengths of tangents drawn from an external point to a circle are equal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.184,
            0.564,
            0.262
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Proof : We are given a circle with centre O, a point P lying outside the circle and two tangents PQ, PR on the circle from P (see Fig. 10.7). We",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are required to prove that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { P Q } = \\mathrm { P R }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.266,
            0.564,
            0.364
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For this, we join OP, OQ and OR. Then",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { O Q P }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "and",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle  ORP"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "are right angles, because these are angles between the radii and tangents, and according to Theorem 10.1 they are right angles. Now in right triangles OQP and ORP,",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.596,
            0.163,
            0.89,
            0.305
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.596,
                0.163,
                0.89,
                0.305
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.699,
                0.323,
                0.8,
                0.344
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 10.7"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.652,
                0.366,
                0.898,
                0.385
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "(Radii of the same circle)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.429,
            0.366,
            0.538,
            0.385
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm { O Q = O R }"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.434,
            0.39,
            0.537,
            0.409
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm { O P } = \\mathrm { O P }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.791,
            0.391,
            0.898,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(Common)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.416,
            0.205,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore,",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.395,
            0.415,
            0.897,
            0.435
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { \\scriptsize ~ O Q P } \\cong \\Delta \\mathrm { \\scriptsize ~ O R P }\\tag{RHS}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.442,
            0.202,
            0.462
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This gives",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.432,
            0.44,
            0.898,
            0.462
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{PQ} = \\mathrm{PR}\\tag{CPCT}"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.486,
            0.203,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Remarks"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.511,
            0.865,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. The theorem can also be proved by using the Pythagoras Theorem as follows:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.535,
            0.682,
            0.555
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{PQ}^{2}=\\mathrm{OP}^{2}-\\mathrm{O} \\mathrm{Q}^{2}=\\mathrm{OP}^{2}-\\mathrm{OR}^{2}=\\mathrm{PR}^{2} \\text { (As OQ=OR) }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.561,
            0.318,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "which gives PQ = PR.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.585,
            0.898,
            0.626
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Note also that",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle OPQ = \\angle OPR"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Therefore, OP is the angle bisector of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { Q P R }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e., the centre lies on the bisector of the angle between the two tangents.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.632,
            0.37,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us take some examples.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.663,
            0.562,
            0.722
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 1 : Prove that in two concentric circles, the chord of the larger circle, which touches the smaller circle, is bisected at the point of contact.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.727,
            0.563,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution : We are given two concentric circles",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { C } _ { \\mathrm { i } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { C } _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "with centre O and a chord AB of the",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " larger circle "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{C}_{1}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "which touches the smaller circle",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { C } _ { z }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "at the point",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { P }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(see Fig. 10.8). We need to prove",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { A P } = \\mathrm { B P } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.829,
            0.563,
            0.868
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us join OP. Then, AB is a tangent to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { C } _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "at P and OP is its radius. Therefore, by Theorem 10.1,",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.874,
            0.362,
            0.893
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_24.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm { O P \\perp A B }"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.615,
            0.669,
            0.858,
            0.821
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 25,
              "bbox": [
                0.615,
                0.669,
                0.858,
                0.821
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_25.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 26,
              "bbox": [
                0.687,
                0.833,
                0.786,
                0.854
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 10.8"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
